Task #919: Backfill pgvector embeddings for listings, services, products

Problem
- Migration 20260417200000_pgvector_embeddings.sql added vector(1536) columns
  + match_embeddings / find_similar_* / semantic_search RPCs but every
  existing row had embedding = NULL, so the recommendation engine silently
  degraded to in-memory cosine.

Changes
- supabase/functions/generate-embeddings/index.ts: bumped per-call default
  limit (100 -> 500) and per-target cap (200 -> 1000) so each cron tick
  drains a meaningful chunk of NULL-embedded rows. Function logic
  unchanged otherwise — it already targets listings, seed_products,
  marketplace_services, profiles via the AI_EMBEDDING adapter.
- supabase/migrations/20260501500000_backfill_embeddings_cron.sql (new):
  * monitored_backfill_embeddings_cron() wraps the dispatch via the
    existing monitored_http_dispatch logger.
  * pg_cron schedule 'backfill-embeddings-cron' every 10 minutes.
  * BEFORE UPDATE triggers on listings, marketplace_services, and
    seed_products that NULL the embedding when contributing text columns
    change, so edited rows get re-embedded on the next tick.
  * Best-effort initial dispatch so the first batch starts immediately.
  * embedding_coverage_report() RPC for ops verification (per-table
    total / embedded / null / coverage_pct), service_role only.

Notes / deviations
- Done criterion "verified end-to-end via vector-similarity-search" was
  not directly testable: that edge function is still a stub
  (file header references task #226). The recommendation engine's actual
  consumer path is match_embeddings, which now has populated rows to
  return. Filed follow-up #932 to replace the stub.
- Filed follow-up #933 to alert on embedding coverage regressions using
  the new embedding_coverage_report() RPC.

